DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/eve
 nts/2026/10/27/guarini-walk-around-occom-pond-9/\nhttps://apply.gs.dartmou
 th.edu/register/?id=42382272-6ab3-4860-928a-fd732d14ec63\nhttps://guarinig
 rad.dartmouth.edu\n\nDescription:\nWalk Around Occom Pond\nJoin the Associ
 ate Dean of Guarini Graduate Student Affairs for a reflective walk around 
 Occom Pond\, followed by a coffee or tea break at Ramekin. This event offe
 rs a chance to connect with fellow graduate students\, postdocs and facult
 y in a relaxed\, natural setting\, promoting well-being and community spir
 it. You can receive a $6 coupon for Ramekin and a Dartmouth Outing Guide B
 ook (limited to one each).\nMeet in front of the Guarini School\, Anonymou
 s Hall – across from Ramekin Cafe.\nGuariniGrad Dialogues\nare a series 
 of events designed to bring graduate students\, postdocs\, and faculty tog
 ether in informal settings to foster empathy\, understanding\, and a deepe
 r sense of community. By creating spaces where differing views\, perspecti
 ves\, and circumstances can be shared and appreciated\, these dialogues ai
 m to strengthen connections within the Dartmouth community and foster a se
 nse of belonging.\n*Guarini graduate students include all PhD\, MA\, MALS\
 , MET\, and MFA students\; and MS students in Engineering\, Computer Scien
 ce\, and Earth Sciences.\n\nSponsor / organizer: GuariniGRAD\n\nAudience: 
 Guarini graduate students and postdocs\n\nSource: Guarini\n\nWhy this was 
 included: food keyword near service context in summary\n\nFood availabilit
 y is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
