DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82938\nhttps://apply.gs.dartmouth.edu/register/?id=54dc7fb2-0f2c-
 4198-b63a-245dbddac3b0\nhttps://irving.dartmouth.edu/education/graduate-st
 udents/master-energy-transition-degree\nhttps://irving.dartmouth.edu/educa
 tion/master-energy-transition-degree/info-sessions-admissions-events\n\nDe
 scription:\nAccelerate Your Impact on the Clean Energy Transition\nRegiste
 r for the On-Campus Info Session\nThe world is building a cleaner\, more r
 esilient energy future — and that shift needs people who can bridge tec
 hnology\, business\, and policy. Dartmouth’s\nMaster of Energy Transiti
 on\n(MET) degree program is designed to train exactly those leaders.\nJoi
 n us for an info session to see what makes the MET different\, and find ou
 t if it's the right next step for you.\nWhat to expect:\nMeet the people b
 ehind the program — our faculty director\, program director\, and MET te
 am\nLearn about the MET faculty\nTake an inside look at our interdiscipli
 nary curriculum and project-based courses\nDiscover how we connect you wi
 th expert mentors through Dartmouth’s powerful alumni network\nGet a pre
 view of our career treks\, where MET students meet energy leaders on the g
 round in Houston and San Francisco\nWalk away with the full picture on app
 lying — process\, tuition\, and financial aid\nLunch will be served\, so
  bring your appetite! We'll close with a live Q&A\, so bring your questio
 ns!\n💡\nBonus:\nAttend the session\, and we'll waive your MET applicat
 ion fee.\nSave your spot and take the first step toward powering the futur
 e.\nRegister for the On-Campus Info Session\nThis Info Session is open to 
 the Dartmouth community. We also offer\nonline Info Sessions\nfor all inte
 rested students.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Arthur L. Irving Institute for En
 ergy and Society\n\nAudience: Alumni\, Faculty\, Postdoc\, Staff\, Student
 s-Graduate\, Students-Undergraduate\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was i
 ncluded: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service context
 \n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details
