BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:University Seminar: Debt and Credit
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T121500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T134500
DTSTAMP:20261025T223712Z
UID:dartmouth-82864@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82864\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScNjqTASzpqvVofOM
 AB46-ZkIfyqc55GyPD3H9VIe-RuoqpFw/viewform\n\nDescription:\nUniversity Semi
 nar on Debt and Credit\nwill convene twice per term over the coming year.\
 nThe seminar takes up debt and credit as frameworks that shape economic an
 d institutional life\, moral reasoning\, and social relations. Debt and cr
 edit function as financial instruments\, of course\, but they also work as
  metaphors and organizing principles across religion\, law\, education\, m
 edicine\, and environmental policy. Our aim is not to arrive at a unified 
 thesis but to build an ongoing forum where colleagues can share work in pr
 ogress\, test ideas\, and see how a shared conceptual vocabulary connects 
 otherwise distant fields. We are hoping for a genuinely interdisciplinary 
 group\, and no disciplinary vantage point is off the table.\nA\ncatered lu
 nch by Salubre will be provided.\nPlease click\nhere\nto confirm your inte
 rest and let us know about any dietary restrictions. If you are not able t
 o make this meeting but would like to remain on the mailing list for infor
 mation about future meetings\, please also use the form to confirm interes
 t.\n\nSponsor / organizer: French and Italian Department\, Leslie Center f
 or the Humanities\, Religion Department\n\nAudience: Alumni\, Faculty\, Po
 stdoc\, Staff\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was included: explicit food
 -service wording\; food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability 
 is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T223712Z
LOCATION:Haldeman 246
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=82864
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food\, Home\, and Words: A zoom conversation with Kim Thúy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T153000
DTSTAMP:20261025T223712Z
UID:dartmouth-83010@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=83010\n\nDescription:\nKim Thúy is one of the most compelling vo
 ices in contemporary Francophone literature. Through her personal and lyri
 cal writing\, she explores themes of migration\, memory\, identity\, and t
 he experience of rebuilding one’s life in a new country. Her debut novel
 \,\nRu\n\, which draws on her family’s experience as Vietnamese refugees
 \, received the Governor General’s Literary Award for French-language fi
 ction and the Grand Prix littéraire Archambault. She has since published 
 several acclaimed works\, including\nMãn\nand\nVi\n\, which explore the c
 omplex connections between food\, memory\, displacement\, and belonging. H
 er first play\,\nẤm\n\, premiered at the Théâtre du Nouveau Monde in f
 all 2025.\nShe will be joining the French 18 students for a conversation o
 n food and life.\n\nSponsor / organizer: French and Italian Department\, L
 eslie Center for the Humanities\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n
 \nWhy this was included: food or meal keyword in title\n\nFood availabilit
 y is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T223712Z
LOCATION:Dartmouth Hall 105
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://home.dartmouth.edu/events/event?event=83010
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
